:July 22, 2025
- puts now handels more thsn one parameter.
- Macros now work at a rudementary level.
  Because the is np compilation step, they
  are not expanded until they are
  encountered. The plan right now is to
  unwind the stack and splice the expanded
  macro into whatever list is being run
  through. Tgis will involve mutation pf the
  list sort of, but it should be safe, and in
  a away isn't ne cessarily umsafe mutation,
  it may still be tread safe, even though we
  are not dealing with multiple threads, just
  a side note, if done correctly. This seems
  to me to be the only way to remember the
  expansion, which is the goal of the macros,
  witjout having an independent upfront pass,
  which really seems like an argous journey.
  i think this will work out ok, but for the
  time being macros can be defined and
  expanded. mufn is the main example macro
  right now, ans is usex to define puts. More
  work to follow on this.
- List and Vector now share a common abstract
  base class AbstractList. The abstract base
  is not meant to be instantiated directly,
  but combines with with the sub classes
  Vector and List to create whole useable
  classes, with all shared functionality
  centralized in the abstract base, unique
  functionality on the sub classes. The is a
  much improved design.
- Switched back to an object centric design
  for List and Vector. Hopefully we'll see
  the benifits of fp in bubblescript, but js
  really isn't designed for it out of the
  box, at least how we were doing it. Trying
  to design list and vector around functions
  was really more of an experiment, and the
  experimwnt served it's purpose. This
  appears to be a part of the core which
  benifits from oo, and probably willcontinue
  to. List and Vectors are now terminated and
  initialized with emptyList and emptyVector
  respectivly, also reflective of Clojures
  design.
- List renamed to Vector, Bubbles renamed to
  List. This no reflects the Cloujure names,
  and better reflects standard name
  expectations. De facto. This should reduce
  at lot of confusion. We had gotten kind of
  carried away.

